From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jacob McSwain <jacob@mcswain.dev>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:55:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): a socket kept through a restart closes once,
 at the next gateway

gateway.restart_socket_close_delay_seconds (0 = off; with restart_listener_hold_seconds): a Webapp WebSocket kept through the restart wait no longer closes when the stop ends its session. The session ends there as before (the app gets a disconnect and runs its teardown before the stores close), but the close frame waits until the gateway that took over answers health, plus this many seconds, then goes out as 1012. Its client's one reconnect then reaches the new gateway directly, instead of a socket the old listener relays and closes again when the relay window ends: two closes per rollout became one. Frames the client sends meanwhile are never read, so a retried call runs once.
